# Q1: the long-context SDPA decode sweep (optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_tp4_long/sdpa_tp4_long.py), on card M alone: the served K64j call (G8B2,
# flags 0x23: two entries of 8 tokens x 6 query heads on 1 KV head, 16 cores per entry, 32 of 110 cores active) at the FOUR-CARD per-chip
# shape, timed against every candidate configuration at 32k / 64k / 131k / 262k (families 33,024 / 65,792 / 131,328 / 262,400 keys) for one
# user and for four, plus a mixed-context and a skewed-context four-user case. Arms (the names QWEN_FAST_TP4_SDPA takes): served, grid8x4,
# grid8x10, grid11x4, grid4x8 (placement only), multi (one G16 launch for all users), rowsplit (G4B4 per user) and ra (KV read-ahead,
# flags 0x2B). Every arm is compared with the served arm as int16 bits, row by row, in the same process, and the served arm's per-user bit
# hashes are recorded; timing is on a trace of 8 steps replayed 10 times, in 5 rounds with a seeded arm order, paired per round against the
# served arm (an eager burst is the fallback if a trace cannot be captured). One card, no mesh, no collectives: the cardm step runs card M
# only and needs no reset before it (A0 freed the cards); after it H1 resets all four.
# THE IMAGE: tp4-next-3a, the four-card image on the rig now. The harness needs an image that CONTAINS THE SERVED SDPA GRAFT (K64j); it
# mounts no graft of its own. It records the installed op binary's sha256 and holds it to the K64j pin in this checkout's build script
# (build-c2-serving-image.sh, read at run time: nothing is spelled in this template), and fails the run with NO-DECISION if the image has
# another graft or a launched program has no [QWEN-SDPA] factory line. The image need NOT contain sdpa_long_tp.py: the harness mounts it.
# Read: sdpalong-<stamp>.json in the cardm results and the verdict line 'SDPA_TP4_LONG verdict=PASS|FAIL|NO-DECISION ...': per case and arm
# the exact flag (differing_rows 0), the paired ratio against served per round, GB/s (K and V bytes read over the step time; DRAM is about
# 405 GB/s), trace_equal; per arm a fit t = fixed_us + per_chunk_us x busiest-core chunks over the one-user cases; and winners: the fastest
# arm that is exact on every case of a kind (u1, u4, mixed, skewed). Pass: the served arm ran in every case, its liveness control moved
# (cur_pos one chunk past E changes the output), every output finite, every factory line present, at least one case timed.
# NOTHING IS APPLIED by this job: a winner goes to QWEN_FAST_TP4_SDPA (profile c2-packed-tp4-best-sdpa) only after a later window proves it in the
# serving gate on an image built from this branch; multi, rowsplit and ra are measured here but are not servable yet.
# Hang risk: rowsplit and ra run flag sets that have never run at one KV head; the sweep runs them after the safe arms in every case, has a
# 300 s per-step watchdog that writes the partial report and exits 124, and the harness prints the target-card reset line on 124 / 137.
# Never cancel this job while it runs (root-owned logs); the next job's reset heals the cards.
# OPTIONAL: its product is data; a failure or a hang does not stop the window.
# Duration (estimate): 40-50 min (about eight programs compile once each; the host builds up to 0.6 GB of K/V for the four-user 262k case;
# the container timeout is 50 min and the sweep stops cleanly 10 min before it, listing what it did not reach).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sdpa-long window: copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit
# of tp4/sdpa-long and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_tp4_long/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--users 4
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
